  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes QFT-based quantum arithmetic primitives that reduce ancilla usage: an integer comparator using 1 ancilla instead of n+1 and ~2n^2 controlled-rotation gates, a quantum-state comparator requiring ~4n^2 CR gates, and a modular adder using 1 reusable ancilla with 8 QFT/IQFT blocks and about 5n^2 CR gates. These circuits enable Shor-style modular arithmetic using about 2n+2 qubits but are presented only as theoretical resource analyses without hardware experiments.",
